    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0352" n="1186" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 657.119/455</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schmedeman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-22T12:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 22, 1918, noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>324. For Dye [from War
                    Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 8. Your No. 1, Legation 727, May 15, 7 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d294-f1"/>
                    We will adopt the procedure which you state has been adopted by British and
                    which involves issuing export licenses against certificates issued by
                    associations prior to May 10, provided associations confirm these in writing to
                    Allied Trade Committee. You will obtain from associations already organized a
                    written declaration that until new agreements can be negotiated they will
                    consider their former agreements <pb facs="0353" n="1187" xml:id="pg1187"/> with
                    Great Britain as applicable to imports from United States, subject, however, to
                    such modifications as are necessitated by the terms of the recently concluded
                    commercial agreement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
